# {{ProductName}}

{{Description}}

This is an add-in for Siemens TIA Portal. Once installed it adds its own entries to the
TIA Portal context menus; there is nothing to start separately.

## Requirements

- TIA Portal V{{TiaVersion}} or higher
- TIA Portal Openness must be installed (it is part of the TIA Portal setup)
- Your Windows user must be a member of the local group `Siemens TIA Openness`
{{AdditionalRequirements}}

## Installation

Choose either of the two equivalent ways to register the add-in with TIA Portal:

- **Copy manually:** close TIA Portal, then copy `{{ProjectName}}.addin` into your
  per-user add-in folder, for example
  `C:\Users\<your user name>\AppData\Roaming\Siemens\Automation\Portal V{{TiaVersion}}\UserAddIns`.
- **Import from within TIA Portal:** start TIA Portal, open **Options → Add-Ins**, and use
  the **Import** action to select `{{ProjectName}}.addin`. TIA Portal copies it into the
  same per-user folder for you.

Either way, finish the activation:

1. Start TIA Portal (if not already running) and open a project.
2. Open **Options → Add-Ins**. The add-in `{{ProductName}}` is listed there with the
   status *Deactivated*.
3. Set the status to *Activated* and confirm the security prompt.

The add-in stays activated for this TIA Portal installation until you deactivate it again.

